import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE, ADS_ON } from '../lib/site';
---
<Page title="Privacy policy" description="What data FBA Tactics, its host and, when enabled, its advertising provider collect; how ad cookies work; consent in the EEA, UK and Switzerland; and your choices." kicker="Legal" updated="November 11, 2026" lede="No accounts, comments, forms that send data to us, newsletter or analytics. If you email us, we use your message only to reply and to fix errors you report. Site search and calculators run in your browser. What is collected is limited to our host and, once switched on, our advertising provider.">
  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>{SITE.publisherName}{SITE.publisherLocation && <>, {SITE.publisherLocation}</>}, publisher of fbatactics.com. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>The site's files are served by GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc.). When you load a page, GitHub's servers receive technical data such as your IP address, browser and the page requested, and may log it for security and operation. We do not receive or use those logs. See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.</p>
  <h2>Advertising (Google AdSense)</h2>
  {ADS_ON ? <p>This site shows ads served by Google through Google AdSense.</p> : <p>This site intends to show ads served by Google AdSense. <strong>At the time of this version, no advertising code runs on the site.</strong> The points below apply from the day ads are switched on, when this page will be re-dated.</p>}
  <ul>
    <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or other websites.</li>
    <li>Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visit to this site and/or other sites on the Internet.</li>
    <li>You can opt out of personalized advertising in <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>, or opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">www.aboutads.info</a>.</li>
    <li>When ads are served, Google and its partners may set or read cookies, use web beacons and receive your IP address and device identifiers. Vendors other than Google that may serve or measure ads are named in the consent message shown in the EEA, UK and Switzerland.</li>
    <li>How Google uses information from sites that use its services: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Visitors in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland</h2>
  <p>Before advertising cookies are set or personal data is used for ads, visitors from these regions see a consent message from Google's certified consent management platform (AdSense "Privacy &amp; messaging"). You can accept, refuse or choose options, and change your choice later from the privacy settings link shown on the page once the message is active.</p>
  <h2>US state privacy laws</h2>
  <p>We do not sell personal information for money and hold no customer database. Advertising cookies placed by Google may count as "sharing" for cross-context behavioral advertising under some state laws; you can limit personalized ads through the links above or by blocking third-party cookies in your browser.</p>
  <h2>Cookies and storage set by this site</h2>
  <p>No cookies. One local-storage value, <code>fbt-consent</code>, remembers your choice in the cookie banner (“Allow personalized ads” or “Non-personalized ads”); you can change it from the <strong>Cookie settings</strong> link in the footer. Choosing “Non-personalized ads” tells Google to serve only non-personalized ads. Non-personalized ads are not based on your past behavior, but Google still uses cookies or similar identifiers with them for frequency capping, aggregated ad reporting and to combat fraud and abuse. While advertising is off, the banner does not open by itself. See the <a href="/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>If you email us we receive your address and message, use them only to reply or correct the site, and delete correspondence within 24 months unless it documents a correction.</p>
  <h2>Children</h2><p>The site is written for business sellers and is not directed at children under 13.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2><p>Depending on where you live you may have rights to access, correct, delete or object to processing of your data. For email correspondence contact us; for hosting logs or advertising data use GitHub's and Google's channels linked above.</p>
  <h2>Changes</h2><p>We update this page when our practices change, including the day advertising is switched on, and change the date at the top.</p>
</Page>
